    <section aria-labelledby="faq-translation-heading" style="margin-bottom:3.5rem;">
      <div class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Multilingual</div>
      <h2 id="faq-translation-heading" class="section-heading" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">Languages &amp; Translation</h2>

      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);">

        <div style="padding:1.75rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Can I post in a language other than English?</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">Yes. You are welcome to post in any language. Other members can use the <strong>Translate</strong> link that appears beneath your post to read it in their own language.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.75rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.6rem;">How do I translate a post written in another language?</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">When a post is written in a language that differs from your interface language, a <strong>Translate</strong> link appears beneath it. Click it and the translated text replaces the original in-page. To see the original again, click <strong>Show original</strong>.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">Note: the Translate link does not appear on posts already written in your interface language.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.75rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Does translation happen automatically?</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">No. Translation is on-demand — you trigger it yourself by clicking the Translate link on an individual post. Posts are not translated automatically when you open a topic.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.75rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.6rem;">How do I change the forum's interface language?</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">The forum interface — menus, buttons, navigation — can be displayed in over 49 languages. To change it:</p>
          <ol style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Click your profile picture in the top-right corner of the forum.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Select <strong>Preferences</strong>.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Go to the <strong>Interface</strong> tab.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Choose your language from the <strong>Interface Language</strong> dropdown.</li>
            <li>Click <strong>Save Changes</strong>.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.75rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.6rem;">What is the difference between the interface language and post translation?</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">These are two separate features. The <strong>interface language</strong> controls how the forum's menus and buttons appear to you — it does not affect post content. <strong>Post translation</strong> converts the text of an individual post into your language on demand. Posts are always stored in the language they were originally written in.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.75rem 0;">
          <h3 style="font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Why don't I see a Translate link on some posts?</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0;">The Translate link only appears when a post is detected as being in a language different from your current interface language. If a post is written in the same language as your interface setting, no Translate link is shown — no translation is needed.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:2rem;">
